      "raw": "<p>When I was creating my oversized cards, I wanted an &quot;H&quot; icon that moved in-line with the rest of the text because I thought it could be a pain to always have to reposition the &quot;H&quot; every time I made a change to the text. &nbsp;So I found a font with a cartoony H, and a dingbats font that had a circle, then adjusted the kerning in Photoshop so that the two were displayed on top of each other. &nbsp;With that, I could copy/paste my &quot;H&quot; icon into any block of text and know it would always hold its position.</p><p>Having said that, I think the actual &quot;H&quot; icon looks better than my solution.</p>",
